<title>JAPAN: Japan gives licence to two more foreign brokerages.</title>
<headline>Japan gives licence to two more foreign brokerages.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) said on Tuesday that it had given South Korea's Daishin Securities Co Ltd and Jefferies (Japan) Ltd permission to conduct brokerage business in Japan.</p>
<p>MOF said the addition of the two firms brought the total number of foreign brokerages operating in Japan to 57,  with 74 offices.</p>
<p>Jefferies (Japan) is a unit of Jefferies Group Inc of the United States.</p>
